.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-001-auto-run-specified.md:8:  \"entry_surface\": \"E1\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-001-auto-run-specified.md:10:  \"prompt\": \"Convene a council to choose a rate-limit strategy for the slug API described in .opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target/spec.md, then recommend one. :auto --packet=.opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target --max-rounds=1\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-001-auto-run-specified.md:12:  \"fixture\": \".opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:3:description: \"Code-facing README for .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts.\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:19:This README documents the code-bearing folder `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts` so operators can understand its role without opening every source file first. It follows the sk-doc skill README structure while staying focused on code navigation.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:39:Start with `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md` for runtime routing and workflow boundaries.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:44:rg --files .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:60:| sk-code alignment | Points reviewers at OpenCode naming, header, error-handling, and type-discipline checks. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:81:| sk-code surface | OPENCODE | Applies OpenCode TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Shell, and config conventions. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:91:User request: Check .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts for sk-code and README coverage.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:112:| [`sk-code/SKILL.md`](../../../sk-code/SKILL.md) | OpenCode coding standards and verification routing. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v2.0.0.0.md:22:- Mirrored the runtime-agent contract across the OpenCode, Claude, and Codex agent surfaces.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:17:- `mode-registry.json` — every mode now carries the canon core fields: `packetKind: \"workflow\"`, `grandfatheredFolderMismatch: false` (folder == packetSkillName for all modes), and a well-formed `toolSurface` (all seven modes are mutating loop/host orchestrators; research additionally grants WebFetch for outward investigation). The three-tier discriminator and every `advisorRouting` projection block are unchanged.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:24:- `PARENT_HUB_CHECK_STRICT=1 parent-skill-check .opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows` — canon invariants pass (3d/3f/5/7a/8a).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:45:**Step 1: Invoke it.** The council offers two surfaces. Pick the one that fits your workload.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:51:python3 .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill_advisor.py \"run an ai council for the login refactor\" --threshold 0.8\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:74:node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs specs/042-pipeline \\\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:83:node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/advise-council-completion.cjs specs/042-pipeline\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:138:`behavior-benchmark/` (ACB scenarios) measures what an executor model actually does at the `/deep:ai-council` command surface under realistic vague/concise prompts: whether it convenes diverse seats (scored on **persisted seat artifacts**, since the common council is in-CLI with no task dispatch), how it presents, whether it stalls, and its latency versus a Claude baseline. Contracts + baselines live here; run evidence and the cross-mode scorecard live in the `033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks` packet.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:174:A: Two of three seats must agree on the material plan direction, and the critique pass must find no new high-severity blocker. If critique surfaces a blocker, the leading plan is not converged regardless of seat agreement. The rule prevents both false consensus and popularity contests.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:182:A: No. All seats inside one round must use the same CLI executor. Seat diversity within a round comes from different models or reasoning lenses on that CLI, not from mixing providers. If you want a different provider's vantage, add a second dedicated round. This keeps each round's sandbox, tool surface and output schema consistent.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:194:| README structure | `python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md --type readme` reports zero issues |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:195:| Skill package structure | `python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/quick_validate.py .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council` exits 0 |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v2.1.0.0.md:12:- Release-cleanup spec folder at `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/116-deep-skill-evolution/000-release-cleanup/004-deep-ai-council` with 4 JSON schemas and `resource-map.yaml`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:1:First release of `deep-ai-council` as a dedicated skill. Council deliberation moves out of `system-spec-kit` and into its own package, the runtime agent is renamed from `multi-ai-council` to `deep-ai-council` across all three runtimes, the advisor learns to route council prompts to the new skill, and the planning-only boundary is enforced through scoped-write helpers that only ever touch packet-local `ai-council/**` artifacts. Two spec packets ship behind this release: 101/001 created the skill surface, 101/003 expanded references and tests to fully document the agent contract.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:3:> Spec folders: `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/101-deep-multi-ai-council-skill/{001-deep-ai-council-skill-creation, 003-deep-ai-council-reference-expansion}` (Level 1 each)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:15:The new `deep-ai-council` skill owns council activation triggers, smart routing across eight council intents, the planning-only operational boundary, and the rules that make council reports reproducible. The skill stays codebase-agnostic, so any project can dispatch a council without inheriting Webflow or OpenCode-specific patterns.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:21:The runtime agent now ships as `@deep-ai-council` across all three runtime mirrors (OpenCode, Claude, Codex). The agent body documents the 9-step workflow from RESOLVE through DELIVER, the dispatch depth rules (Depth 0 parallel via `Task`, Depth 1 sequential via `sequential_thinking` MCP), and the persistence protocol that calls writer functions in a fixed order so every artifact lands with an audit event.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:63:Six references cover the day-to-day surface: `output_schema.md` (the markdown report contract the parser enforces), `folder_layout.md` (packet-local artifact tree), `state_format.md` (append-only JSONL events), `command_wiring.md` (caller-owned post-dispatch persistence), `seat_diversity_patterns.md` (lens combinations and vantage targets), and `convergence_signals.md` (two-of-three-agree rule and escape hatches). Four further references were added in 101/003 to lift agent-body logic into the reference layer: `scoring_rubric.md` documents the 5-dimension rubric, multi-round deliberation, and the Hunter / Skeptic / Referee adversarial cross-critique; `depth_dispatch.md` codifies Depth 0 vs Depth 1 detection and no-recursive-counciling rules; `failure_handling.md` walks through timeouts, all-seats-fail, contradiction-without-resolution, and insufficient vantage diversity; `anti_patterns.md` lists the eleven council anti-patterns with detection cues and recovery actions.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:81:Targeted vitest coverage already exists at `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/multi-ai-council-*.vitest.ts` and continues to pass after the rename, the persistence library refactor, and the sk-code style alignment.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:97:No new top-level commands ship in this release. The agent is dispatched through normal Task delegation patterns, and the persistence helper at `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs` runs as a CLI wrapper for callers that need to persist a captured council report from outside the agent context.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:108:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md`                                   | Created — sk-doc template aligned, 8 numbered sections, 4-pattern smart router, 8-intent routing model   |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:109:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/README.md`                                  | Created — HVR style, 10 numbered sections, 252 lines                                                     |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:110:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/description.json`                           | Created — discovery metadata, version 1.0.0                                                              |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:111:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/graph-metadata.json`                        | Created — skill graph node, depends-on system-spec-kit, sibling deep-research                            |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:112:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/output-schema.md`                | Created — markdown report contract for the persistence parser                                            |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:113:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/folder-layout.md`                | Created — packet-local artifact tree                                                                     |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:114:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/state-format.md`                 | Created — append-only JSONL event semantics                                                              |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:115:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/command-wiring.md`               | Created — caller-owned post-dispatch persistence patterns                                                |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:116:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/seat-diversity-patterns.md`      | Created — Strategy lenses table, 5 diversity requirements, task-type auto-selection (264 lines)          |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:117:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/convergence-signals.md`          | Created — two-of-three-agree default, escape hatches, validator graduation note                          |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:118:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/scoring-rubric.md`               | Created — 5-dimension rubric, Hunter/Skeptic/Referee, conflict resolution matrix (343 lines)             |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:119:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/depth-dispatch.md`               | Created — Depth 0/1 detection, parallel/sequential, no-recursion (280 lines)                             |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:120:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/failure-handling.md`             | Created — timeouts, all-fail, contradiction, insufficient vantage (260 lines)                            |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:121:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/anti-patterns.md`                | Created — 11 council anti-patterns with detection cues and recovery actions (161 lines)                  |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:122:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs`              | Created — thin CLI wrapper delegating to lib                                                             |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:123:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/d