ncode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib` so operators can understand its role without opening every source file first. It follows the sk-doc skill README structure while staying focused on code navigation.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:39:Start with `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md` for runtime routing and workflow boundaries.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:44:rg --files .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:60:| sk-code alignment | Points reviewers at OpenCode naming, header, error-handling, and type-discipline checks. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:80:| sk-code surface | OPENCODE | Applies OpenCode TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Shell, and config conventions. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:90:User request: Check .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib for sk-code and README coverage.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:111:| [`sk-code/SKILL.md`](../../../../sk-code/SKILL.md) | OpenCode coding standards and verification routing. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:6:This prompt pack renders the per-iteration context for the `@deep-review` LEAF agent (native executor) or a CLI executor (e.g. `opencode run`). Tokens use curly-brace syntax and are substituted by `renderPromptPack` before dispatch.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:28:Load `.opencode/skills/sk-code/code-review/references/review-core.md` before final severity calls.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:5:Renamed the skill `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/` → `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/` and the agent `.opencode/agents/deep-ai-council.{md,toml}` → `.opencode/agents/ai-council.{md,toml}` across all three runtime mirrors. Family moved from `deep-loop` to `sk-util` per the parent spec.md §2 rationale: the Council is a planning sentinel skill (closer to sk-prompt's role) rather than an autonomous-loop executor like deep-research/deep-review which iterate to convergence. Behavior, trigger phrases, MCP wiring, council graph projection, and deliberation logic are all unchanged — this is a pure identity refactor.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:12:- Directory: `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/` → `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/` (via `git mv` — history preserved).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:14:  - `.opencode/agents/deep-ai-council.md` → `.opencode/agents/ai-council.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:20:| Surface group | Files |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:24:| Sibling skill graph edges | `cli-devin/graph-metadata.json`, `cli-opencode/graph-metadata.json` (already pointed at sk-* — unchanged); `deep-research/graph-metadata.json`, `deep-agent-improvement/graph-metadata.json`, `system-spec-kit/graph-metadata.json`, `system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json` (edges updated) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:27:| Council MCP test surface | `system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/multi-ai-council-runtime-parity.vitest.ts`, `council-helpers-smoke.vitest.ts`, `council-playbook-anchor-integrity.vitest.ts`, `multi-ai-council-audit-trail.vitest.ts`, `multi-ai-council-permission-scope.vitest.ts`, `multi-ai-council-rollback.vitest.ts`, `multi-ai-council-persist-artifacts.vitest.ts`, `scripts/test-council-matrix.sh` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:29:| Agent body skill-path references | each `ai-council.{md,toml}` body now references `Read(.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md)` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:32:| Skills index | `.opencode/skills/README.md` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:35:- Compiled `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill-graph.json` via `skill_graph_compiler.py --export-json --pretty`. Result: 22 skills, 6 families, `deep-ai-council` now appears in the `sk-util` family alongside `sk-prompt-small-model`, `sk-doc`, `sk-git`, `sk-prompt`, and `deep-agent-improvement`. `deep-loop` family is now strictly `deep-research` + `deep-review`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:38:- `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md` + `v1.1.0.0.md` — historical version state under the original name.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:39:- `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/101-deep-multi-ai-council-skill/**` (entire originating packet — 63 files documenting the work that created the skill).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:40:- `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/108-auto-review-quick-wins-verdict-markers-logging/**`, `110-auto-review-stretch-config-dedup-gates/**`, `113-cli-devin-prompt-quality/**` historical refs in past packets.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:49:| Live-surface rename | `rg \"deep-ai-council\"` on live allow-list | 0 hits |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:50:| Historical surfaces preserved | `git diff --stat` on 101/** + 108/** + 110/** + 113/** + sibling skill changelogs | unchanged |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:51:| Rename history | `git log --follow .opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md` | traces back to original `deep-ai-council/SKILL.md` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:54:| Advisor surfaces new name | `advisor_recommend({input: \"multi-seat AI Council deliberation\"})` | deep-ai-council at confidence **0.95** (above 0.7 threshold) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:59:- `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/116-deep-skill-evolution/` (Phase 115 of skilled-agent-orchestration track, 6-phase decomposition: preflight + skill-rename + 4-runtime-agent-rename + cross-skill-edges-and-code + root-docs-hooks-and-readmes + reindex-validate-reconcile).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:60:- Sister rename arc: `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/114-small-ai-model-optimization/007-sk-prompt-small-model-rename/` (sk-small-model → sk-prompt-small-model, shipped 2026-05-21) — established the mechanical-rename pattern that 115 reused.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:61:- Shared reference: `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/rename-pattern.md` — captures the reusable workflow for repo-wide rename refactors.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:28:When `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=1`, the directive shells out to `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub system-deep-loop --prompt \"<task>\"` before running the registry-driven routing above. The front door is a thin, promoted delegate: it resolves `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs` and calls `resolveRoute(hubId, taskText)`, which authorizes a compiled decision only when BOTH the tri-state runtime flag permits it AND `system-deep-loop`'s promoted activation manifest (`.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/010-live-activation/activation/system-deep-loop/manifest.json`) reports `servingAuthority: \"compiled\"`. Any other combination, or any error while resolving, prints the legacy sentinel and `system-deep-loop` routes unchanged. As of this writing, `system-deep-loop`'s promoted manifest already reports `servingAuthority: \"compiled\"` and `shadowOnly: false` — the tri-state flag is the sole gate currently withholding compiled serving by default.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:36:A served compiled decision returns one of four actions — `route` (use the returned `targets`), `clarify` or `defer` (disambiguate before proceeding), or `reject` (refuse) — which the `system-deep-loop` directive follows directly. The same decision, when returned inside `advisor_recommend`, is additionally attached to that recommendation's `compiledRoute` field and threaded into brief rendering as `metadata.compiledRouteSummary`; see [`advisor-recommend.md`](../../../system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/mcp-surface/advisor-recommend.md) for the shared advisor-side consumption path.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:40:`node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-status.cjs --hub system-deep-loop` reports `system-deep-loop`'s current serving posture as one stable JSON record with a `causeCode`: `compiled-serving` when the flag permits, the manifest authorizes, and the engine actually routes; `flag-off` or `legacy-authority` when the manifest is ready but the flag or manifest authority withholds it (expected drift, not breakage); `missing-manifest` when no promoted manifest exists; `engine-throw` when the flag and manifest both authorize compiled serving but the engine itself fails (a genuine break, distinct from expected drift). See [`feature-flag-governance.md`](../../../system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/governance/feature-flag-governance.md) for the `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING` flag-governance entry.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:50:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md` | Shared | Carries the opt-in compiled-routing directive `system-deep-loop` follows. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:51:| `.opencode/bin/compiled-route.cjs` | Script | Promoted CLI front door the directive shells out to. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:52:| `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs` | Shared | Tri-state flag parsing and the manifest serving-authority gate. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:53:| `.opencode/